body: "## Boundary and documented goal\n\nReproduced on main `eac19c5bf3ceb7a82f1e958ac97bef4d9af16fc6`, Node v24.19.0/Linux, with the exact committed lockfile and `@unbrained/pm-cli@2026.10.13`. Source blobs were verified against GitHub and rebuilt distribution bytes matched the committed distribution. This is a real installed-CLI result using a disposable Git repository and items created by the actual SDK, not a mocked host.\n\n[README lines 73–76](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/eac19c5bf3ceb7a82f1e958ac97bef4d9af16fc6/README.md#L73-L76) specify file-overlap ranking first, followed by lifecycle/priority and existing limits/packing. The [feature owner pm-context-ax7z](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/eac19c5bf3ceb7a82f1e958ac97bef4d9af16fc6/.agents/pm/features/pm-context-ax7z.toon) and merged [PR #151](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/pull/151) describe the same file-focused selection goal.\n\n## Reproduction and controls\n\nCreate nine Task items in a fresh tracker, all with:\n- status `open`\n- title `\"X\".repeat(100)`\n- no body\n- equal-length IDs\n\nOne item, `focus-best-000`, has priority 4 and a file link to `src`. The other eight, `focus-next-000` through `focus-next-007`, have priority 0 and a file link to `src/a.ts`.\n\nRun the installed extension:\n\n```sh\npm context-pack --files src/a.ts --files src/b.ts --without-neighborhood --format json\npm context-pack --files src/a.ts --files src/b.ts --without-neighborhood --format json --max-items 1\npm context-pack --files src/a.ts --files src/b.ts --without-neighborhood --format json --max-items 1 --id focus-best-000\npm context-pack --files src/a.ts --files src/b.ts --without-neighborhood --format json --max-items 1 --limit 1\n```\n\nResults:\n1. No item cap: `focus-best-000` is first, with `matched_files: [\"src/a.ts\",\"src/b.ts\"]`; the eight others each match only `src/a.ts`\n2. `--max-items 1`: only `focus-next-000` is emitted\n3. Same budget + explicit best ID: `focus-best-000` is emitted\n4. Same budget + `--limit 1`: `focus-best-000` is emitted\n\nAll nine identity projections cost exactly 29 estimated tokens; their summary/full projections each cost 32. The one-slot budget is 220. The highest-overlap item comfortably fits; its loss is not a legitimate oversized-item fallback or a smaller-item optimization. Nine required identities total 261 tokens, exposing the ordering error during budget selection.\n\nMinimal deterministic public-helper reproduction:\n\n```js\nimport { buildContextPack, createSdkPacker } from \"./dist/index.js\";\n\nconst best = {\n  id: \"focus-best-000\", title: \"X\".repeat(100),\n  type: \"Task\", status: \"open\", priority: 4,\n  files: [{ path: \"src\" }],\n};\nconst next = Array.from({ length: 8 }, (_, i) => ({\n  id: `focus-next-00${i}`, title: \"X\".repeat(100),\n  type: \"Task\", status: \"open\", priority: 0,\n  files: [{ path: \"src/a.ts\" }],\n}));\nconst globalRelevanceOrder = [...next, best];\nconst pack = buildContextPack([best, ...next], {\n  fileFocus: { root: \"/repo\", files: [\"src/a.ts\", \"src/b.ts\"], refresh: \"\" },\n  neighborhood: false,\n  maxItems: 1,\n  packer: createSdkPacker(globalRelevanceOrder, globalRelevanceOrder),\n});\nconsole.log(pack.items.map(item => item.id));\n// Actual: [\"focus-next-000\"]; expected: [\"focus-best-000\"]\n```\n\nThe same failure occurs through the real CLI with SDK-created records, without injecting a packer. Both positive controls above pass before the overlap-selection assertion fails.\n\n## Cause and impact\n\n[Command setup](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/eac19c5bf3ceb7a82f1e958ac97bef4d9af16fc6/index.ts#L1495-L1502) builds the packer from the entire corpus's general relevance ordering. [File selection](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/eac19c5bf3ceb7a82f1e958ac97bef4d9af16fc6/index.ts#L522-L529) ranks by overlap, but [createSdkPacker](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/blob/eac19c5bf3ceb7a82f1e958ac97bef4d9af16fc6/index.ts#L1213-L1247) sends the earlier general ranks to token-budget selection. When not all required identities fit, an item matching fewer changed files can displace the best-overlap item. The final slice preserves the order only among survivors.\n\nAn agent requesting a small file-focused pack can therefore lose the item covering the most of its working set. The matching and tracking data remain correct; no data loss or tracker corruption was observed.\n\n## Suggested acceptance\n\n- Preserve file-focused ordering through budget-constrained focus selection\n- Cover equal-cost candidates whose combined identities exceed the budget\n- Assert the highest-overlap item survives when it individually fits\n- Keep the explicit-ID and limit-one controls and existing neighborhood behavior\n- Verify JSON and explain report the same emitted selection\n\n## Duplicate and scope check\n\nAll 152 pre-existing issues/PRs across all states and current canonical PM issues/features were reviewed. Closed [#136](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-context/issues/136) concerns dependency-kind/direction projection, not ranking or packing. The relevant feature owner is pm-context-ax7z. All 17 authored file-focus tests pass; this is an independent gap in budget-pressure coverage. No source implementation changes, dependency-pin changes, live integrations, or publication were performed."
